These terms govern the relationship between Fluster GmbH, Zürich (hereinafter "we" or "us"), and the users and organizations that use our services (hereinafter "you" or "customer").

"Services" means the software as a service (SaaS) nullish and the related applications and interfaces.

By creating an account or using our services, you accept these terms.

## Scope

These terms apply to the Cloud plan and to anyone using nullish. For a dedicated instance or an on-premises installation, the agreement we sign with you takes precedence. These terms apply wherever it says nothing.

The source code of nullish is open source under the MIT license. These terms cover the service we run, not the code.

## Account

You need an account to use nullish. Give accurate information.

Each organization has its own subscription and its own admins. Admins decide who has access and with which role.

## Use of the services

For the duration of the agreement, we provide nullish to you for paid use.

You're responsible for keeping your nullish account and your API keys secure. Any liability on our part for data loss or damage resulting from a failure to do so is excluded.

You're solely responsible for the lawful and proper use of the software in accordance with applicable laws. This includes, in particular, the use of the functions for keeping your accounting.

Help texts and instructions in our services don't replace professional advice or training by a fiduciary. We're not liable for damage resulting from incorrect use of the services.

You may not use our services for illegal or otherwise unauthorized purposes.

You're solely responsible for all content you transmit through your nullish account, as well as for all activities carried out in the organizations you created.

Automated use of nullish is only permitted through the REST API and the MCP server, within their limits.

## Software functionality

We reserve the right to remove or modify any functionality of the software at any time, without notice and without giving reasons.

## Availability

We strive to ensure the highest possible availability of our services. However, due to technical reasons, scheduled or unscheduled maintenance, or force majeure, we can't guarantee uninterrupted availability of the software. Maintenance and outages are announced on [nullishstatus.com](https://nullishstatus.com) whenever possible.

## Trial

A new organization may start with a free trial. If it ends without a plan, the organization is locked: its data can't be accessed until it has a plan again.

## Prices and payment

The prices are listed on the [pricing page](/en/pricing/), in Swiss francs, excluding VAT.

A subscription is paid in advance for the chosen period, monthly or yearly, and renews automatically. Payments are processed by Stripe.

If a payment fails, a banner shows the date the organization will be locked. Update the payment method before then and everything goes on as usual.

## Cancellation

You can cancel at any time under **Subscription**. The subscription keeps running until the end of the period already paid. Periods already started aren't refunded.

## Account termination

We reserve the right to delete accounts, organizations and the associated data at any time if we detect activities we consider illegal, undesirable or otherwise unacceptable.

## Your data

Your data stays yours. We process it only to provide nullish, and acting on your behalf. The [privacy policy](/en/privacy/) explains how.

When an admin deletes an organization, it becomes read-only, at the latest at the end of the period already paid. It's deleted for good, with all its data, 30 days later.

nullish doesn't replace your duty to keep your business records. Under Swiss law, you must keep them for 10 years. Make sure you keep a copy.

## AI assistant

The assistant's answers are generated by an AI model and can be wrong. Check them before relying on them. They don't replace the advice of a fiduciary or a tax expert.

We don't use your data to train AI models.

## Unlawful content

You undertake to indemnify us against all claims of third parties based on the data you store, and to reimburse us for all costs we incur due to possible violations of the law.

We're entitled to block your data immediately if there's a reasonable suspicion that it's unlawful or infringes the rights of third parties. Such a suspicion exists in particular if courts, authorities or other third parties notify us of it. We inform you immediately of the block and the reason for it, unless authorities prohibit us from doing so. The block is lifted as soon as the suspicion is fully dispelled.

## Liability

Within the framework of the statutory provisions, we exclude any liability towards you (or any third party), in particular for the fulfilment of our contractual and non-contractual obligations and for the loss of data, including for negligence. This exclusion of liability also applies to damage caused directly or indirectly by the use of nullish.

If we involve auxiliary persons to fulfil our contractual obligations, we're solely responsible for instructing them carefully. Warranty and liability are otherwise excluded to the fullest extent permitted by law. This exclusion of warranty and liability also applies in particular to intent and gross negligence.

In all cases, regardless of the basis of liability, our liability is limited to the amount of the fees you paid in the twelve months before the damage occurred.

Warranty and liability in relation to third-party software and services, in particular banks and payment providers, are excluded to the fullest extent permitted by law.

## Intellectual property

All intellectual property rights to our services, in particular to nullish and its website, remain ours. The source code of nullish is published under the MIT license, whose terms apply to it.

## Confidentiality

We undertake to keep confidential all confidential matters that come to our knowledge in the preparation, implementation and fulfilment of this agreement, in particular your business secrets, and not to pass this information on to third parties without your authorization. This applies to any unauthorized third party, unless the disclosure is necessary for the proper fulfilment of our contractual obligations.

## Contractual amendments

We're entitled to change our services and/or any part of the agreement (including these terms) and/or the agreed fees, prices and charges, including subscription fees, at any time. You'll be informed of this in a suitable manner, e.g. via a message in nullish, by email or by post.

If the changes represent a significant deterioration of the conditions from your point of view, you're entitled to extraordinary termination with a notice period of 14 days at the time of the change.

## Severability

Should any provision of these terms be or become invalid or void, this doesn't affect the validity of the remaining provisions. In such a case, the invalid or void provision is replaced by a new, legally permissible provision that comes as close as possible to its economic meaning and purpose. The same applies should a gap in these terms arise.

## Governing law and jurisdiction

These terms, including matters of their formation and validity, are governed by Swiss law, excluding the conflict of laws rules and international agreements.

The exclusive place of jurisdiction for all disputes arising from or in connection with these terms is Zürich.

